    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0373" n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/50: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-02T14:00:00-00:44">March 2, 1942—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:54 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. From McBride.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>First plane arrived yesterday overnighted at Harbel. Pilot enthusiastic
                        about landing field. Some difficulty encountered because of fadeouts but
                        radio contact Harbel to Accra for plane direction finally
                        established.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Obtained permission from Liberian Government February 17 for Harbel radio
                        station to communicate directly with Fisherman Lake and other necessary
                        points. Such communication to be exclusively for direction of plane traffic.
                        This permission, which is outside their contract, granted to the Firestone
                        station only temporarily until Panair can establish its own radio facilities
                        at air field. This latter should be given prompt attention.
                        [McBride.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
